title: Veeam: Replica
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a replica of a Veeam Backup & Replication server, collected
 via the Veeam special agent. It reports the replica's state, type, platform,
 source job, creation time and ID. Reading replicas requires the Veeam Backup
 Administrator or Veeam Restore Operator role.

 By default, the check is {OK} if the replica is ready, being processed or under a
 SureBackup test, {WARN} if it is failed over, failing back or ready to switch
 back to production, and {CRIT} if a failover failed. The state for each of these
 replica states is configurable. A replica state not known to the check is
 always {UNKNOWN}.

 CDP replicas are not monitored: Veeam reports no state for them.

discovery:
 One service is created for each replica reported by the API, except CDP replicas.

item:
 The name of the replica, followed by the first 8 characters of its ID in
 parentheses, since replica names are not unique in Veeam.
